---
description: Spec-driven development. Work from docs/specs; one task, one commit, one check; ask instead of guessing.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Changes bigger than a typo have a spec in `docs/specs/NNN-<slug>.md`. It is the source of truth. Rules: `docs/specs/README.md`.
- Take the lowest-numbered unclaimed §6b task whose needs are met; write your name in Claim.
- One task = one commit (subject `NNN-Tn: ...`) = one check. Run the check before the next task. Fail: fix it inside this task.
- Change only the files the task names. Never build anything in the spec's §4 "Out of scope".
- Missing detail: ask, never guess. Stop that task, add a §5 row with the question, report it in the RESPONSE BLOCK, and take a task that does not depend on it.
- Branch `spec/NNN-<slug>`; one draft PR per spec with each check's output pasted. Fill the RESPONSE BLOCK, including PROBLEMS and STATE.
